  "content": "<table align=\"center\" border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\">\n<tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\">\n<div>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px;\">\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\">\n<tr>\n<td align=\"left\" style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\">\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"line-height: 1.6em; font-size: 40px; font-weight: 200; color: #fafafa;\">🚀 <strong>Frontend</strong> Focus</td></tr></table>\n<div style=\"color: #fafafa;\"><p>#​763 — October 21, 2026 | <a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/191824/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #fafafa; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\">Read on the web</a></p></div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</table>\n</td></tr></table>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\">\n<a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/191779/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/w_1280,e_sharpen:60,q_auto/v1792580550/hxa80wdvuurmobkzyw5x.png\" style=\"line-height: 100%;\" width=\"640\"/></a>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\"><p>Everyone's Interop 2027 Wishlists</p></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p>Last week we shared that you can now <a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/191779/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\">rank the Interop web platform proposals for 2027</a>. Since then, plenty of folks have shared their own rankings and explained their choices:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>⭐ <a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/191780/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\">Josh Comeau's <em>The Future of CSS</em></a> – Josh's top ten, from CSS functions and <code>corner-shape</code> to anchored container queries and scroll-triggered animations, each with live demos, current browser support, and tips you can use today. A particularly good place to start.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>🔎 <a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/191782/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\">Sara Soueidan's picks</a> put accessibility first. It's a privilege, she notes, that we get to influence what browser makers work on. <code>focusgroup</code> is her top pick.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>✏️ <a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/191783/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\">Declan Chidlow's 13 features</a> – SVG improvements on top, followed by the CSS <code>reading-flow</code> and <code>reading-order</code> properties.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>📝 More picks from <a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/191784/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\">Stuart Robson</a>, <a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/191785/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\">Eric Meyer</a>, <a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/191786/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\">Ana Rodrigues</a>, and <a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/191787/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\">Tyler Sticka</a>, and 🦋 <a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/191788/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\">this Bluesky thread</a> has even more.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Inspired to submit your own? <a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/191789/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\">Rank about ten proposals you'd like to see prioritized</a>. The Firefox team says that's enough to provide useful input.</p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<div style=\"margin-top: 14px; margin-bottom: 8px;\"></div>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;\">\n<a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/191778/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\"><img height=\"140\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/c_limit,w_480,h_480,q_auto/copm/e8bf0b4e.png\" style=\"padding-top: 12px; padding-left: 12px; line-height: 100%;\" width=\"140\"/></a>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/191778/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306; font-size: 1.15em; line-height: 1.25em; font-weight: 400;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"www.meticulous.ai\">Would You Let Your AI Agent Grade Its Own Homework?</a></span> — Agents write code faster than ever. They even review their own work. But who’s reviewing them? Dropbox, Notion &amp; ElevenLabs don’t take the risk. With Meticulous, every change is exhaustively verified, with zero developer effort.</p>\n<p>Meticulous <span style=\"margin-left: 4px; font-size: 0.9em; color: #997 !important; padding: 1px 4px;\">sponsor</span></p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;\"><span>🗳️</span> <a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/191790/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"survey.devographics.com\">The State of HTML 2026</a></span> — The annual survey returns to measure the awareness and adoption of HTML features and browser APIs. This year covers Web Components, progressive enhancement, AI, and more. It takes less than 15 minutes and you can learn new things just by taking it.</p>\n<p>Devographics </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/191791/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"webkit.org\">Safari Blocks 'Identity Resolution' Tracking Infrastructure</a></span> — Cross-site cookies are long gone in Safari, so trackers moved to 'identity resolution' where third parties get the email address you type into forms and turn it into a cross-site, cross-device tracking ID. Safari now blocks them at the domain level.</p>\n<p>Wilander, Wolfe, and Finkel (WebKit) </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px;\">\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 1.2em;\">⚡️</span> <span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.2em;\">IN BRIEF</span></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>⚠️ If PHP runs anywhere behind your sites: <a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/191792/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\">PHP 8.5.12, 8.4.27, 8.3.36 and 8.2.35 fix two critical bugs</a> that allow unauthenticated remote code execution. Update now, <em>mod_php</em> installs especially.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>🌐 <a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/191793/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\">Chrome 157 is in beta</a> with <code>corner</code> shorthands, a <code>&lt;string&gt;</code> value for <code>text-overflow</code>, and <code>anchor-valid</code>. Chrome 156 went stable this week with CSS <code>random()</code>.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>🚫 <a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/191794/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\">Chrome has finished deprecating the <code>unload</code> event</a>: handlers no longer fire by default, so use <code>pagehide</code> or <code>visibilitychange</code> instead.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 1.2em;\">📙</span> <span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.4em;\">Articles, Opinions &amp; Tutorials</span></p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\">\n<a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/191795/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/w_1280,e_sharpen:60,q_auto/v1792585763/nrxh8gwtp2lom2spe99p.png\" style=\"line-height: 100%;\" width=\"640\"/></a>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/191795/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"jakearchibald.com\">JPEG XL vs AVIF for Web Use-Cases</a></span> — Now that JPEG XL has landed in all major browsers, Jake took the format for a spin, benchmarking it against AVIF. There's a lot of detail here with some good takeaways. You might also be surprised at <a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/191796/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\">what you can cram in under 200 bytes</a> with JPEG XL.</p>\n<p>Jake Archibald </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/191797/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"www.smashingmagazine.com\">Embracing Playful Imperfection with CSS's <code>random()</code> Function</a></span> — A look at how to approach adding some <a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/191798/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\">randomness</a> into our projects, and whether it makes sense on the web. The demos here show off some ideas, like organic typography, bouncing letters, and splayed cards.</p>\n<p>Brecht De Ruyte </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/191799/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"www.miris.com\">Photorealistic 3D in the Browser Without the Rendering Overhead</a></span> — Learn how radiance fields and spatial streaming bridge real-time photorealistic 3D to the web with just 2 lines of Three.js.</p>\n<p>Miris <span style=\"margin-left: 4px; font-size: 0.9em; color: #997 !important; padding: 1px 4px;\">sponsor</span></p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/191801/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"ishadeed.com\">Fitting an Element's Height to Its Background Pattern with <code>calc-size()</code></a></span> — A repeating pattern cut off at the bottom is a classic annoyance. Ahmad uses <code>calc-size()</code> (Chromium only for now, Safari soon) with <code>round()</code> to snap an element's auto height to a multiple of the tile height.</p>\n<p>Ahmad Shadeed </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/191802/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"web.dev\">Core Web Vitals Now (Experimentally) Count Soft Navigations</a></span> — Most sites won’t notice, but navigation-heavy SPAs should see scores improve, with Search Console switching over when it goes stable next year.</p>\n<p>Annie Sullivan (Google) </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/191803/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"www.craigabbott.co.uk\">Using Math to Balance Your Heading Styles</a></span> — Craig outlines a simple system for styling heading levels using a modular scale.</p>\n<p>Craig Abbott </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;\">▶  <a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/191804/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"www.youtube.com\">Do We Really Need <code>alpha()</code>?</a></span> — We now have three ways to lower the opacity of a color in CSS. Kevin has the details, highlighting what the <code>alpha</code> function brings to the table in particular.</p>\n<p>Kevin Powell </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.0em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/191825/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306; font-size: 1em !important; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">WCAG 3: A Different Future for Accessibility</a></span> — Why binary pass/fail made WCAG 2 a ceiling, and how WCAG 3 aims to make conformance a floor.\n  <br/><span style=\"color: #5a5a5a; margin-top: 4px; font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.6em !important;\">Léonie Watson (TetraLogical)</span>\n</p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.0em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/191805/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306; font-size: 1em !important; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Compression and Concatenation on the Web</a></span> — A hands-on look at how gzip, brotli and zstd each cope with concatenation on the web.\n  <br/><span style=\"color: #5a5a5a; margin-top: 4px; font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.6em !important;\">Phil Eaton</span>\n</p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.0em; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/191806/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306; font-size: 1em !important; font-weight: 500 !important;\" target=\"_blank\">Do Web Components Have a Future If Nobody is Writing Them?</a></span>\n<br/><span style=\"color: #5a5a5a; margin-top: 4px; font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.6em !important;\">Nolan Lawson</span>\n</p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 1.2em;\">🧰</span> <span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.4em;\">Tools, Code &amp; Resources</span></p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\">\n<a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/191807/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/w_1280,e_sharpen:60,q_auto/v1792586072/dn5ggcb9ehrb9a895kpd.png\" style=\"line-height: 100%;\" width=\"640\"/></a>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;\"><span>📊</span> <a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/191807/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"chartist.dev\">Chartist 2.0: This Lightweight SVG Charting Library Is Back</a></span> — A freshly modernized SVG charting library that you style with CSS. It originally popped up in 2014, but <em>\"went stale\"</em>. It's back with a composable API, server-side rendering, and still remains small. <a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/191808/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\">There's a migration guide</a> for existing users.</p>\n<p>Gion Kunz et al. </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/191809/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"www.bram.us\">A DevTools Extension for Debugging CSS Scroll-Triggered Animations</a></span> — Adds a pane to Chrome DevTools that draws a scroll-triggered animation's activation and active ranges on a minimap, shows a live status light, and lets you edit the ranges in place. <a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/191810/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\">Chrome Web Store</a>, or <a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/191811/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\">source here</a>.</p>\n<p>Bramus Van Damme </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/191812/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"try.expo.dev\">Mobile AI Infrastructure for Web Devs Who Code with Agents</a></span> — Point the agent you use for the web at iOS and Android. Expo takes care of the native builds and the trip to the stores.</p>\n<p>Expo <span style=\"margin-left: 4px; font-size: 0.9em; color: #997 !important; padding: 1px 4px;\">sponsor</span></p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\">\n<a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/191814/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/w_1280,e_sharpen:60,q_auto/v1792585320/q67zejhisepeytmieq5p.png\" style=\"line-height: 100%;\" width=\"640\"/></a>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/191814/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"pele.run\">Pele: Mermaid Diagrams as Lightweight, Themeable SVG</a></span> — A zero-dependency renderer for the <a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/191815/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\">Mermaid</a> diagram syntax that outputs responsive SVG you can theme with CSS variables. It claims to be a sixth the size of Mermaid.js. You can <a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/191816/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\">try the playground here</a>.</p>\n<p>Steph Ango (Obsidian) </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/191817/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"pour.dev\">pour: A Free Accessibility Checker &amp; WCAG Audit Tool</a></span> — Available as a browser extension or bookmarklet. Run it on any page to see an overlay with violations categorized as critical, serious, moderate, minor, etc.</p>\n<p>David Yarham </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;\"><span>🤖</span> <a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/191818/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"lighthouse-md.com\">Lighthouse for Claude Code: Turn PageSpeed Audits into a <code>CLAUDE.md</code> Fix Plan</a></span> — Enter a URL and this tool will run a Google PageSpeed Insights and Lighthouse audit and generate instructions for Claude Code tailored to the audits.</p>\n<p>Baris Kocdur </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/191819/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"3dsvg.design\">3dsvg: The Easiest Way to Turn SVGs Into 3D</a></span> — A web-based editor that takes an uploaded SVG, text, or drawing and renders the flat image as 3D. Exports in a 3D software compatible format such as GLB, STL, etc.</p>\n<p>Renato Costa </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 1.2em;\">🔤</span> <span style=\"font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.4em;\">A font that annotates itself</span></p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\">\n<a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/191820/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/w_1280,e_sharpen:60,q_auto/be9dkecdoetpsmnqiuxg.jpg\" style=\"line-height: 100%;\" width=\"640\"/></a>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;\"><a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/191820/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"furifont.antfu.me\">Furifont: A Japanese Font That Draws Its Own Furigana</a></span> — Furigana, the small readings above kanji, usually mean using <code>&lt;ruby&gt;</code> markup or JavaScript. Anthony's font does it with OpenType features alone! <a href=\"https://frontendfoc.us/link/191821/rss\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: #D94306;\" target=\"_blank\">Repo here</a>.</p>\n<p>Anthony Fu </p>\n</td></tr></table>\n<table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><td style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;\"></td></tr></table>\n</div>\n</td></tr>\n</table>\n",
